  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and cool weather is expected through the rest of \nthe week, with patchy frost possible across the North Country and \nwestern Southern Tier at times.\n\nGradual eastward progression of an upper level trough and associated \nclosed low will pass across the Midwest to the Ohio Valley this \nafternoon and tonight. As the trough enters the east coast, a \ncoastal low will develop late this week. Overall, surface high \npressure will dominate across eastern Canada where dry weather will \npersist with easterly flow across the eastern Great Lakes into the \nweekend.\n\nAs the surface high settles further across the region tonight, clear \nskies and light winds will be favorable for radiational cooling, and \nresult in another cool night. Temperatures in the mid to upper 30s \nare likely across the Tug Hill region, which will support some \npatchy frost. Otherwise, low temperatures in the low to mid 40s are \nexpected across the lower elevations.  \n\nHigh temperatures will gradually increase day to day through Friday.",
